Package: howbig
Title: Empirical, Method-Aware Power Analysis for Differential Network Analysis
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:c(
    person("Margaret", "Janiczek", , "mjaniczek@umass.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Raji", "Balasubramanian", , "rbalasub@umass.edu", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Sample-size and power calculations for differential network
    analysis, grounded in a precomputed simulation grid across sample size,
    feature count, perturbation type, and estimation method. Power is the
    sensitivity for truly differential edges at a false-discovery-rate
    target, reported alongside the achieved false discovery rate. Answers
    come from the grid where possible, by interpolation along its swept
    axes, or by on-demand simulation, and every answer records how it was
    produced. A network-native, method-aware analogue to 'pwr'.
